<header><p class="enc-kicker">Religion / idea · period</p><h1 class="enc-title">Late Bronze Age</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Late <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bronze-age">Bronze Age</a> is the period of roughly the sixteenth to the twelfth centuries BCE in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/near-east">Near East</a> and eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mediterranean">Mediterranean</a>. It was an era of great territorial powers, including the Egyptian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-kingdom-of-egypt">New Kingdom</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hittite-empire">Hittite Empire</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mitanni">Mitanni</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/babylon">Babylon</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/assyrian-empire">Assyria</a>, linked by diplomacy, trade and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chariot">chariot</a> warfare. The period ended with the widespread upheavals known as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/late-bronze-age-collapse">Late Bronze Age collapse</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/late-bronze-age.jpg" alt="Late Bronze Age" width="320" height="204" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Chris 73 · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Minoan_copper_ingot_from_Zakros,_Crete.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
